# Format: path_glob::symbol_glob  # reason
#
# Every line below is an upstream symbol that is absent from our copy of the
# same file, captured as a BASELINE on 2026-08-07 against upstream/main.
# It is a snapshot of existing divergence, NOT an assertion that each line is
# correct. The mix is roughly:
#
#   * upstream features this fork never ported
#   * modules the fork deliberately rewrote (sample_utils, apc, cache,
#     server/generation) where upstream's helper names simply do not apply
#   * genuine hunks dropped by past merges -- the failure mode documented in
#     docs/upstream-gaps.md
#
# Entries are listed per symbol rather than per file on purpose: a file-wide
# `apc.py::*` would also hide the NEXT symbol silently lost from apc.py, which
# is exactly what this check exists to catch.
#
# Shrinking this file is good. When you port or restore something, delete its
# line. Nothing should ever be ADDED here without a specific reason replacing
# the generic one.


